{"id":"namibia-loop","title":"Namibia: desert and Etosha loop","who":"Classic route · self-drive with a rooftop tent","when":"May to October (dry, cool nights)","vehicle":"4x4 with rooftop tent, 12–16 days","kind":"4x4","color":"#c2410c","summary":"The classic self-drive: from Windhoek over the escarpment to the red dunes of Sossusvlei, along the foggy Atlantic coast at Swakopmund and Cape Cross, through Spitzkoppe and the rock art of Damaraland, to the waterholes of Etosha. Long gravel roads, few people, huge skies.","sources":[{"label":"This Is Pure Felicity: Namibia road trip, 4,460 km (April 2026)","url":"https://thisispurefelicity.blogspot.com/2026/04/namibia-road-trip-4460-kilometers-of.html"},{"label":"Lizy Travels the World: Namibia road trip day by day","url":"https://lizytravelstheworld.com/namibia-road-trip-two-week-itinerary-day-by-day/"},{"label":"Rough Guides: planning a self-drive safari in Namibia","url":"https://www.roughguides.com/namibia/self-drive-safari/"}],"approximate":"A common two-week loop; the gravel roads are the router's choice.","km":2175,"bbox":[13.9525,-24.6602,17.3424,-18.7852],"stops":[{"name":"Windhoek","place":"Windhoek, Namibia","at":[-22.5776,17.0773],"text":"Pick up the 4x4, stock up on water and food.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Christ_Church_in_Windhoek%2C_Namibia.jpg/500px-Christ_Church_in_Windhoek%2C_Namibia.jpg","page":"Windhoek","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christ_Church_in_Windhoek%2C_Namibia.jpg","credit":"Christoph Strässler","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Sossusvlei","place":"Sesriem, Namibia","at":[-24.4871,15.7985],"text":"Over the Spreetshoogte pass to Sesriem; at dawn, the dunes and the dead trees of Deadvlei. After rain the access roads can flood.","source":{"label":"This Is Pure Felicity (2026)","url":"https://thisispurefelicity.blogspot.com/2026/04/namibia-road-trip-4460-kilometers-of.html"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sossusvlei.jpg/500px-Sossusvlei.jpg","page":"Sossusvlei","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sossusvlei.jpg","credit":"Ikiwaner","license":"GFDL 1.2"}},{"name":"Solitaire","place":"Solitaire, Namibia","at":[-23.8936,16.0063],"text":"A desert stop famous for its apple pie.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Solitaire_%282019%29.jpg/500px-Solitaire_%282019%29.jpg","page":"Solitaire, Namibia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solitaire_%282019%29.jpg","credit":"Hp.Baumeler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Swakopmund","place":"Swakopmund, Namibia","at":[-22.6768,14.529],"text":"Through the Kuiseb canyon to a German-era town in the coastal fog.","source":{"label":"Lizy Travels the World","url":"https://lizytravelstheworld.com/namibia-road-trip-two-week-itinerary-day-by-day/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg/500px-Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg","page":"Swakopmund","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg","credit":"Olga Ernst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Cape Cross","place":"Cape Cross, Namibia","at":[-21.7714,13.952],"text":"Tens of thousands of fur seals on the Skeleton Coast.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Cape_Cross_Seal_Colony.jpg/500px-Cape_Cross_Seal_Colony.jpg","page":"Cape Cross","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cape_Cross_Seal_Colony.jpg","credit":"betty x1138 from NYC, USA","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Spitzkoppe","place":"Spitzkoppe, Namibia","at":[-21.8488,15.2044],"text":"Granite peaks and wild campsites among the boulders.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Spitzkoppe_year_2006.jpg/500px-Spitzkoppe_year_2006.jpg","page":"Spitzkoppe","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spitzkoppe_year_2006.jpg","credit":"Hp.Baumeler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Twyfelfontein","place":"Twyfelfontein, Namibia","at":[-20.5484,14.411],"text":"Thousands of rock engravings in Damaraland; desert elephants nearby.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Twyfelfontein_16.jpg/500px-Twyfelfontein_16.jpg","page":"Twyfelfontein","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Twyfelfontein_16.jpg","credit":"Mike from Vancouver, Canada","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Etosha: Okaukuejo","place":"Okaukuejo, Namibia","at":[-19.181,15.9157],"text":"A floodlit waterhole where rhinos and lions come to drink at night.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Dust_Cloud_in_Etosha_National_Park.jpg/500px-Dust_Cloud_in_Etosha_National_Park.jpg","page":"Etosha National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dust_Cloud_in_Etosha_National_Park.jpg","credit":"Yathin S Krishnappa","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Etosha: Halali","place":"Halali, Etosha","at":[-19.0333,16.4667],"text":"The middle camp, with a waterhole under a rocky hill.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg/500px-Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg","page":"Etosha Pan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg","credit":"Alchemist-hp (talk) (www.pse-mendelejew.de)","license":"FAL"}},{"name":"Etosha: Namutoni","place":"Namutoni, Namibia","at":[-18.8063,16.9417],"text":"An old German fort at the east end of the pan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg/500px-Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg","page":"Etosha Pan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dry_Etosha_Pan.jpg","credit":"Alchemist-hp (talk) (www.pse-mendelejew.de)","license":"FAL"}},{"name":"Back in Windhoek","place":"Windhoek, Namibia","at":[-22.5776,17.0773],"text":"South on tarmac to return the car."}],"legs":[{"by"